# The asset tree is binary art ripped from the upstream release package. Nothing here may ever be
# treated as text:
#
#  - `text=auto` / `eol=lf` would let git normalise line endings. That corrupts PNG/MP3/skel bytes,
#    and the sha256 in cdn/v1/index.json would stop matching what this branch serves.
#  - `diff`/merge can never work on these formats, so they are marked binary outright.
#
# This branch exists to be served by git-mount CDNs (jsDelivr / ghfast / gh-proxy), which deliver
# whatever bytes git holds. Byte fidelity is therefore not cosmetic, it is the contract.
* -text -diff -merge binary

# The five sp-bundle packs are the only files above GitHub's 100 MB blob ceiling, so they
# have to be LFS. The pattern is deliberately narrow: jsDelivr and raw.githubusercontent do
# not resolve LFS, so widening it would turn the whole art tree into 130 B pointers.
assets/local/sp-bundle/*.spart filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
